  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#20245\", \"terminal#20004\"], \"answer\": \"This crash has been reported before. Selecting a font in the Font face box with the arrow keys and pressing Enter crashes Terminal (terminal#20004, terminal#20245). The cause in terminal#20245 is that the font face AutoSuggestBox explicitly unfocuses itself after a keyboard-selected suggestion is committed. A fix, PR #20255, was opened for it. The archive doesn't confirm that it has shipped, and your version 1.25.1912.0 still crashes. Until a build with the fix reaches you, pick the suggestion with the mouse instead of the arrow keys and Enter, which worked in terminal#20004. You can also type the full font name, such as \\\"Berkeley Mono, Hack Nerd Font\\\", or edit fontFace in settings.json. Add your version and the crash details to terminal#20245 so the team knows it still happens after the fix.\"}",
